// ============================================================================
// keybindings.json — shared key bindings for Visual Studio Code and Cursor
// ============================================================================
//
// WHAT THIS FILE IS
//   Custom key bindings, overriding the defaults. Like settings.json, one file
//   serves both editors through symlinks; that file's header lists the four
//   destinations and the editing rules.
//
// WHY IT IS EMPTY
//   Both editors' default bindings are used unchanged. The file exists so that
//   a future binding is version-controlled from the start instead of being
//   created outside the repo.
//
// HOW TO ADD ONE
//   Objects of {"key", "command"}, optionally with "when" and "args":
//       { "key": "cmd+k cmd+t", "command": "workbench.action.selectTheme" }
//   The Keyboard Shortcuts UI (cmd+K cmd+S) shows a command's id; write the
//   binding here rather than through the UI, which edits this file with its
//   own formatting. Bindings are platform-specific in VS Code's sync model
//   but not in this file: use `cmd+` for macOS and `ctrl+` for Linux, or bind
//   both.
// ============================================================================
[]
